            <ArticleTitle>[Management of coronary perforation after percutaneous balloon angioplasty with a new membrane stent].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>948-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 59 year old patient underwent percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty of a de novo stenosis of the proximal right coronary artery. Vessel perforation occurred after balloon angioplasty and was successfully treated by implantation of a new stent graft, which completely covered the perforation without residual leakage. Emergency coronary surgery could, thus, be avoided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
